{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1220,
    "dDurationMs": 4580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "My good friend CGP Grey has made a great video\nabout the practical and philosophical concerns"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5800,
    "dDurationMs": 4370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with teleportation, in particular the concern\nthat when a transporter dismantles the atoms"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10170,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in your body and reassembles an identical\narrangement of atoms somewhere else, perhaps"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13950,
    "dDurationMs": 4270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the disassembled you actually dies and the\nreassembled you is actually a new being that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18220,
    "dDurationMs": 1210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just thinks it’s you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19430,
    "dDurationMs": 4089,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if they simply hadn’t dismantled the\noriginal you, then there’d now be two “you’s”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23519,
    "dDurationMs": 2810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the universe, and which is really you?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26329,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You, or the teleported you?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28279,
    "dDurationMs": 3650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Grey’s video covers these questions really\nwell so if you want more background you should"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31929,
    "dDurationMs": 3801,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "go watch that, but I do have one additional\npiece of information I’d like to point out,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35730,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "something the original creators of Star Trek\nwere definitely unaware of because it was"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39250,
    "dDurationMs": 1660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "discovered in the 90s."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40910,
    "dDurationMs": 2380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that, is quantum teleportation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43290,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Quantum teleportation is the only kind of\nreal teleportation technology we currently"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46800,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have access to, and while I won’t go into\nthe details here the point is you can take"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50600,
    "dDurationMs": 3770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "some particles in a particular arrangement,\nand transfer their exact quantum condition"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54370,
    "dDurationMs": 2380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "onto other particles arbitrarily far away."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56750,
    "dDurationMs": 4420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You might think of it as “sad teleportation”\nbecause the particles don’t move, just their"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61170,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "state – but isn’t that essentially what\na Star-Trek teleporter does, albeit on a larger"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65610,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "scale?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66610,
    "dDurationMs": 3460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sending enough information and energy over\nto the new location to create the exact arrangement,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70070,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or state, of particles that corresponds to\n“you”?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73010,
    "dDurationMs": 4750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And quantum teleportation has one pivotal\nproperty: it is impossible to create an identical"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77760,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "copy of a quantum state without destroying\nthe original – in fact, you HAVE to destroy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81780,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the original arrangement in order to extract\nall the necessary information from it to construct"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85620,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the new, teleported, state."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86620,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, the relevant theorem in quantum mechanics\nis called the “no cloning” theorem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90790,
    "dDurationMs": 4550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, we don’t yet know exactly how brains\nwork to create consciousness, but if the quantum"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95340,
    "dDurationMs": 3210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "states of some electrons somewhere in the\nbrain are critical to perfectly determining"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98550,
    "dDurationMs": 4450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(and thus copying) “you”, then a teleporter\nwould necessarily have to obey the rules of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103000,
    "dDurationMs": 3659,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "quantum teleportation when sending the information\nabout the arrangement of particles that are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106659,
    "dDurationMs": 10001,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "“you” to the new location, and whatever\nwas left behind would definitively *not* be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116660,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you."
    } ]
  } ]
}
